- s1 local MySQL also running idle, consumes 1G buffer pool but memory okay; CPU minimal. Could stop to free CPU/memory. But s1 app service Requires=mysql, so stopping might cause restart issues? `Requires` means if mysql stops, app stops. If we stop mysql after app started, systemd will stop app. So leave s1 MySQL running idle. It may use memory but not CPU. Could lower s1/s3 buffer pool to 128M to free memory for app; not necessary with 3.7G. But s2 DB needs 1G. s1/s3 app memory is small. Leave.

